@startuml
' Figure 27-1: the compile-time translation pipeline. One pass per language:
' language! (OSLF spec) -> LanguageDef (GSLT) -> Dovetail rules -> set-automaton intern
' -> classify -> serialize the three layers -> fail-closed gate -> installed rhoapi::Par.
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #4A5568
  FontColor #1A202C
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
top to bottom direction

title Figure 27-1 — the compile-time translation pipeline (once per language)

rectangle "language! specification\n(an OSLF spec)" as SPEC #C6E0F5
rectangle "LanguageDef\n(the GSLT: types, equations, rewrites)" as LDEF #C6E0F5
rectangle "Dovetail rules-as-data\nRewriteRule<L> carrying Pattern<L>" as RULES #DDEBF7
rectangle "<b>PatternCompiler::intern</b>\nthe set automaton (interned DAG)\nO1/O3 size-optimal quotient = tc(K)" as INTERN #F6C177
rectangle "RhoNetProgram::from_language_def\nclassify each rule (BaseRewrite / AC / ...)" as CLASSIFY #DDEBF7
rectangle "serialize the three layers\nmatching  |  firing  |  congruence" as SERIAL #D6C6EE
rectangle "installed_program_par\n(fail-closed install gate)" as GATE #FDE9C8
rectangle "<b>rhoapi::Par</b>\nthe installed program (the seam to runtime)" as PAR #A7D8B6

SPEC --> LDEF
LDEF --> RULES
RULES --> INTERN
INTERN --> CLASSIFY
CLASSIFY --> SERIAL
SERIAL --> GATE
GATE --> PAR

note right of INTERN #FCF3D0
  The interner is the compile-time partial evaluator:
  structurally-equal sub-patterns share one StateId.
  This is the entire tc(K) computation; the runtime
  pays no pattern-compilation cost.
end note
@enduml
